From cffdad86020f9c7afa6f1c122988af81333cd694 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lmoresi <louis.moresi@anu.edu.au>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 14:04:21 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] An interior ribbon whose cavity runs along the wall is
 placed; only a sliver's gap is refused

A ribbon whose band ended a few cells below a domain wall was refused: the
cavity around the band reached the wall, and the band did not reach it, so
it was neither interior nor an outcrop. On an annulus with a ladder ribbon,
every band whose highest corner lay between 0 and about 2 cells below the
wall was refused, at dips of 15 to 45 degrees and at two cell sizes. A slab
model lost the middle of its dip scan to it.

The wall's vertices are protected from the carve, so the cavity can run
along the wall and keep the wall's edges and labels. Measured with the
refusal removed: every such band is placed, no wall edge loses its label (an
annulus at three dips and two cell sizes, and a box corner where the cavity
runs along two walls), and the cells' smallest angle matches a deep
placement from about half a cell of gap on. Below that the cells filled in
between the skin and the wall become slivers: about 22 degrees at 0.3 cells,
1 degree at 0.01.

So the refusal now applies only when the gap between the band's skin and
the wall is below 0.3 of the wall's cells there (_MIN_WALL_GAP_CELLS; the
cell size is the mean length of the ring's wall edges at the nearest wall
vertex, not the mesh's nominal size). Its message gives the gap in cells and
in mesh units and both ways out: move the band further from the wall, or
closer, so it reaches the wall as an outcrop. The decision is made by the
rank holding the cavity and agreed through the placement's failure gather,
so every rank refuses or places alike, on the gather and the
seam-conforming paths. It replaces the reach-and-distance message for this
case, which no longer fires.

test_0904 (tier B): bands 2.5-3.5 cells below the wall at two cell sizes are
placed inside, the wall keeps its labels, the fault is split, and the cells
beside the wall are no worse than 0.8 of a deep placement's; a band 1.95
cells below is refused with a gap in cells within 0.05 of the geometry's; a
box corner keeps both walls and its corner vertex. test_0865's fixture
(0.67 cells of gap) is now placed.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
